    "lawCode": "Amd §66, Pub Serv L (as proposed in S.8213 & A.2736-A)",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8764\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to consideration of\ncapital expenditures by a utility proposing a major change in rates\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2025,\nC.622\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter to limit the application\nof this bill to a major change in rates and clarifies that the PSC shall\nconsider the operation of the distribution system among other factors\nwhen examining capital expenditures.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 17 of 2025, the Executive and Legislature have\nreached agreement on modifications to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 622 of the Laws of 2025.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2025 amending the public service law relating to\nutility capital expenditures, as proposed in legislative bills numbers\nS.8213 and A.2736-A.\n",
